$t=2$, $\tilde{\theta}_{2}=2\theta(1-\theta)\in (0,\frac{1}{2})$ and $\tilde{\theta}_{2}=2\theta(1-\theta)>\theta=\tilde{\theta}_{1}$. If $\tilde{\theta}_{t}>\tilde{\theta}_{t-1}$ and $\tilde{\theta}_{t}\in(0,\frac{1}{2})$ holds 
for $t=2,\ldots,k-1$, then for $t=k$ we have
\begin{align}
