We adopt a computer-aided approach to prove the lemma. Lemma \ref{lem:mono} shows that the error exponent is strictly increasing in $t$, so we only need to prove the lemma for $t=3$. 




Let $\mathcal{A}(n)\triangleq E_{3}(\hat{\mathcal{T}}_{{\rm SCL}},\mathcal{T},\hat{\alpha} n)$ be the event that $\hat{\mathcal{T}}_{\rm{SCL}}(\hat{\alpha} n)\text{ has a }3\text{-hop error}$. In addition,   let $\mathcal{B}(n)\triangleq\{\hat{\alpha} \in \mathcal{M}\}$ be the event that 
$\hat{\alpha}$ takes the value in a set $\mathcal{M}$, where $\mathcal{M}\subseteq \Psi$ is an appropriately chosen subset of values of $\hat{\alpha}$. Lemma \ref{lem:twoseq} implies that we only need to separately lower bound $K(\mathcal{A}\cap \mathcal{B})$ and $K (\mathcal{B}^{\complement})$. We have
\begin{align}
	K ( \mathcal{A}\cap \mathcal{B})&=\varliminf_{n\rightarrow\infty}-\frac{1}{n}\log \bigg(\sum_{\beta\in \mathcal{M}}\Pr\big(E_{3}(\hat{\mathcal{T}}_{{\rm SCL}},\mathcal{T},\hat{\alpha} n),\hat{\alpha}=\beta\big)\bigg)\\
	&\geq \varliminf_{n\rightarrow\infty}-\frac{1}{n}\log \bigg(\sum_{\beta\in \mathcal{M}}\Pr\big(E_{3}(\hat{\mathcal{T}}_{{\rm SCL}},\mathcal{T},\beta n)\big)\bigg)\\
	&=\min_{\beta\in \mathcal{M}}\varliminf_{n\rightarrow\infty}-\frac{1}{n}\log\Pr\big(E_{3}(\hat{\mathcal{T}}_{{\rm SCL}},\mathcal{T},\beta n)\big)\\
	&=\min_{\beta\in \mathcal{M}}\,\beta\cdot \varliminf_{n\rightarrow\infty}-\frac{1}{n}\log\Pr\big(E_{3}(\hat{\mathcal{T}}_{{\rm SCL}},\mathcal{T},n)\big)\\
