The induced graph $\mathcal{T}(\mathscr{C}_{\mathrm{V}}(\hat{\alpha} n)^{\complement})$ is not necessarily a connected graph, and we assume that it has $k$ components: $\mathcal{T}_{1}$, \ldots, $\mathcal{T}_{k}$. For each component, we 
show that $N(\mathcal{E}(\mathcal{T}_{i}),\mathcal{T}_{i},2)\geq \frac{|\mathcal{V}(\mathcal{T}_{i})|}{2d}$. See Fig.~\ref{fig:packing} for an illustration of this proof.

