Note that the edges in the induced subgraph $\hat{\mathcal{T}}_{{\rm active}}\big(\mathscr{C}_{\mathrm{V}}(\hat{\alpha} n)^{\complement}\big)$ not only contain the unconfident edges, but also contain some confident edges. However, Lemma \ref{lem:confide} shows that the exponent of the event that the confident edges are wrongly estimated is larger than $c_{\rho}K _{{\rm passive}}(\rho)$. Thus, in the following proof, we focus on the unconfident edges in $\hat{\mathcal{T}}_{{\rm active}}\big(\mathscr{C}_{\mathrm{V}}(\hat{\alpha} n)^{\complement}\big)$.

We set $\mathcal{J}(n)\triangleq\{\hat{\mathcal{T}}_{{\rm active}}\big(\mathscr{C}_{\mathrm{V}}(\hat{\alpha} n)^{\complement}\big)\neq \mathcal{T}\big(\mathscr{C}_{\mathrm{V}}(\hat{\alpha} n)^{\complement}\big)\}$ be the event that the learned structure of unconfident nodes is wrong, and $\mathcal{K}(n)\triangleq\{N(\mathscr{C}_{\mathrm{E}}(\hat{\alpha} n)^{\complement},\mathcal{T}(\mathscr{C}_{\mathrm{V}}(\hat{\alpha} n)^{\complement}),2)\leq 12\}$ be 
the event that the 2-packing number of the unconfident edges set is not more than  $12$. Lemma \ref{lem:packnum} then shows that 
\begin{align}
	\varliminf_{n\rightarrow\infty}-\frac{1}{n}\log\Pr\big(\mathcal{K}(n)^{\complement}\big)\geq c_{\rho}K _{{\rm passive}}(\rho).
\end{align}
Then we only need to consider the event $\mathcal{J}\cap \mathcal{K}$. Lemmas \ref{lem:tilpbound} and \ref{lem:numsample} show that there are at least $\big[\hat{\alpha}+3(1-\hat{\alpha})\big]n$ scalar samples for every unconfident node, since Algorithm~\ref{algo:alathe} will distribute $(1-\hat{\alpha})pn$ scalar samples only among $\tilde{p}$ unconfident nodes in the local refinement stage. 

For $\rho\in [0.8,1)$, we will numerically compute the exponent of the event that $\{\hat{\alpha} \neq 0.8\}$. It follows from Table~\ref{table:alpha} that $\hat{\alpha} \neq 0.8$ implies $\hat{\rho}<0.76$. Furthermore, for $\rho=0.8$, we have $\rho-\frac{1-\rho}{5}=0.76$. To show that $K\big(\{\hat{\rho}(\hat{\alpha} n)\leq \rho-\frac{1-\rho}{5}\}_{n\in\mathbb{N}}\big)\geq c_{\rho}K_{{\rm passive}}(\rho)$, we only need to show that $130D(\frac{6\theta}{5}\|\theta)\geq c_{\rho}K_{{\rm passive}}(\rho)$, following the similar procedures of Lemma \ref{lem:rhobound}.
